%% Sequence Diagram 1 - User Authentication (Login)
sequenceDiagram
    actor Staff as Staff Member
    participant UI as Login Form<br/>(login.html / auth.js)
    participant Filter as JwtAuthenticationFilter
    participant Ctrl as AuthController
    participant Mgr as AuthenticationManager
    participant UDS as CustomUserDetailsService
    participant UserRepo as UserRepository
    participant Jwt as JwtService
    participant DB as MySQL

    Staff->>UI: enter username & password, click "Sign In"
    UI->>Filter: POST /api/auth/login {username, password}
    Note over Filter: /api/auth/** is permitAll -<br/>filter passes the request through
    Filter->>Ctrl: login(request, response)

    Ctrl->>Mgr: authenticate(UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken)
    Mgr->>UDS: loadUserByUsername(username)
    UDS->>UserRepo: findByUsername(username)
    UserRepo->>DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?
    DB-->>UserRepo: user row
    UserRepo-->>UDS: User

    alt account disabled or password mismatch
        UDS-->>Mgr: throw / BCrypt mismatch
        Mgr-->>Ctrl: throw BadCredentialsException
        Ctrl-->>UI: 401 Unauthorized {"Invalid username or password"}
        UI-->>Staff: show inline error
    else credentials valid
        UDS-->>Mgr: UserDetails (username, encoded password, ROLE_*)
        Mgr-->>Ctrl: Authentication (authenticated)

        Ctrl->>UserRepo: findByUsername(username)
        UserRepo-->>Ctrl: User
        Ctrl->>Jwt: generateToken(username, role)
        Jwt-->>Ctrl: signed JWT

        Ctrl->>Ctrl: set HttpOnly cookie "dc_token"
        Ctrl-->>UI: 200 OK {user, token, expiresIn} + Set-Cookie: dc_token
        Note over UI,Ctrl: token is also returned in the JSON body -<br/>the browser client relies on the safer HttpOnly<br/>cookie, but a non-browser API client (Postman,<br/>curl, Swagger's Authorize button) uses this<br/>token as "Authorization: Bearer token" instead
        UI-->>Staff: redirect to dashboard.html
    end
